    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (67.19) and **Dylan Beavers** (66.70) anchor our lineup as the premier plays. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** maintains a strong profile despite facing a decent arm in Sean Newcomb, bolstered significantly by his position in the two-hole and an advantageous platoon split. **Dylan Beavers** earns high marks primarily due to his leadoff duties against Tong, where the 10% order bonus and positive platoon splits offset a slight park penalty. While **Will Smith** (65.44) is the only other starter clearing the 60-point threshold, he remains a solid start behind the plate, benefiting from a favorable 4.71 xERA matchup against Lodolo and high-efficiency batting order placement.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the starting lineup with a 32.44 score, landing well below our 40-point floor. While his raw metrics are decent, the combination of a tough matchup against Williams (2.89 xERA) and a lowly #9 spot in the lineup made him an easy exclusion to preserve our precious game caps. We are also closely monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**; while projected for a 53.58, his status remains \"Lineup Pending.\" Should he drop in the order or be scratched, we have depth ready, but his current score reflects a heavy downgrade due to the difficult matchup against Tarik Skubal-caliber pitching, and we will need to pivot if the confirmed order shifts unfavorably.\n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **JJ Bleday** (46.43). He is a marginal start, surviving in the lineup only because his platoon edge against a lefty-heavy profile provides enough stability to keep him out of the bench pile. We are consciously avoiding exposure to high-xERA opponents like Skubal where possible, but given the constraints, we are prioritizing efficiency over raw talent. With **Bryce Harper**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Lawrence Butler** all inactive today, the squad 